            "description": "# What is Crystal Fair?\nCrystal Fair is to assess any model for biased predictions against a particular group (e.g. discriminative outcomes on grounds of race, gender etc.). \n\n## Setup and Installation\nFollow below steps to run it-\n\nStep1: Make sure you are in statistical-fairness directory.\n\nStep2: Load the data and pass required parameters to the Fair object as shown in the snippet.\n``` bash\n# Import Library\nfrom statistical_fairness.main import Fairness\n\n# Import Data\ndf = get_data('income.csv')\n\n# Create Fair Object\nfair_object = Fairness(data: pandas dataframe,\n                       model_type: type of model - multiclass/binary/regression),\n                       previleged_class: in multiclass-> it is a list,\n                                         in binary -> it is a integer (1/0),\n                                         in regression -> it is a threshold\n                       y_pred -> columns name for predictions,\n                       protected_feature -> columns name for protected feature)\nfair_object.get_result()\n```\n\n\n",
